IMPORTANT: This is just an example!

To create your actual proxies.json:
1. Copy this file: cp config/proxies.example.json config/proxies.json
2. Replace all values with your REAL paid proxy credentials
3. Format from your proxy provider should match:
   - ip: Proxy server IP address
   - port: Proxy server port (usually 8080, 3128, or custom)
   - username: Your proxy authentication username
   - password: Your proxy authentication password
   - city: City where proxy is located
   - state: State/Province where proxy is located
   - zip: Postal code of proxy location

Note: The geo-matching algorithm will pair users with proxies
from the same zip code or city when possible.